Audit and fix ClipFlow's Google Search appearance and favicon setup.

Website:
https://clipflow.cliy.me

Brand:
ClipFlow by Cliy

IMPORTANT:
Do NOT redesign the website.
Do NOT change the existing UI, layout, colors, functionality, authentication, backend, or video-processing logic.
Only make SEO, metadata, favicon, structured-data, and crawlability improvements.

GOALS:

1. FIX THE GOOGLE SEARCH RESULT LOGO / FAVICON

Google currently shows a generic globe icon beside the ClipFlow search result instead of the ClipFlow logo.

Inspect the existing favicon setup and fix it properly.

Requirements:
- Use the existing ClipFlow logo if one already exists in the project.
- Do not create a random new logo.
- Make sure the favicon is square and preferably at least 48x48, with a higher-resolution source such as 192x192 or 512x512 if available.
- Prefer PNG or ICO.
- Put the favicon in the correct publicly accessible location.
- Add the correct <link rel="icon"> tag.
- Add apple-touch-icon if appropriate.
- Make sure the favicon URL works directly in production.

For example:

<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/favicon.png">

But first inspect the project's existing assets and use the correct path.

IMPORTANT:
Because the production site is a subdomain:
https://clipflow.cliy.me

the favicon must actually be accessible from that production hostname.

Verify that:

https://clipflow.cliy.me/favicon.png

(or the actual favicon URL) returns the correct image and is not a 404.

2. FIX GOOGLE SEO METADATA

Audit the current <head> in frontend/index.html and make sure the production page has:

- One clear <title>
- One meta description
- Canonical URL
- OpenGraph title
- OpenGraph description
- OpenGraph URL
- OpenGraph image
- Twitter/X card metadata
- Twitter/X title
- Twitter/X description
- Twitter/X image
- favicon

Brand the site consistently as:

"ClipFlow by Cliy"

Recommended title:

ClipFlow by Cliy

Description :
Download and clip any video using direct links from YouTube, Instagram, Twitch, or Twitter. With custom clipping options, download a 10-second clip instead of a whole 4-hour video — 100% free with creator tools.
+
Do NOT keyword stuff.

3. CANONICAL URL

Make sure the homepage has:

<link rel="canonical" href="https://clipflow.cliy.me/">

Do not accidentally canonicalize the page to cliy.me or another domain.

4. OPEN GRAPH

Configure the homepage for proper social previews.

Use:

og:title
og:description
og:url
og:type
og:image
og:site_name

The OpenGraph image must actually exist in production.

For example:

https://clipflow.cliy.me/og-image.png

Only use this path if the file actually exists.

5. TWITTER/X METADATA

Keep Twitter/X metadata because it is only social sharing metadata.

It does NOT connect to the Twitter/X API.

Use:

twitter:card
twitter:title
twitter:description
twitter:image

Use "summary_large_image" if there is an appropriate large social preview image.

6. STRUCTURED DATA

Inspect the existing structured data.

If appropriate, add valid JSON-LD for:

- Organization
- WebSite

Make the relationship clear:

Cliy = organization/brand
ClipFlow = product/site

Do not invent fake social profiles, reviews, ratings, awards, or other information.

Use the real production URL:

https://clipflow.cliy.me/

7. ROBOTS.TXT

Check whether robots.txt exists.

Make sure it does NOT accidentally block:

/
favicon files
CSS
JavaScript
important assets

The production site should be crawlable by Google.

If appropriate, include:

Sitemap: https://clipflow.cliy.me/sitemap.xml

8. SITEMAP.XML

Check whether sitemap.xml exists.

If it does not exist, create the appropriate sitemap for the actual public ClipFlow pages.

Do not put private, authenticated, dashboard, API, temporary, or user-specific URLs into the sitemap.

Use:

https://clipflow.cliy.me/sitemap.xml

9. GOOGLE CRAWLABILITY

Check all of the following:

- Homepage returns HTTP 200
- Googlebot is not blocked
- robots.txt is valid
- canonical URL is correct
- favicon returns HTTP 200
- OG image returns HTTP 200
- sitemap returns HTTP 200
- important CSS/JS is accessible
- there is no accidental noindex
- there is no accidental nofollow
- HTTPS works correctly
- redirects do not send the homepage somewhere unexpected

Check both development configuration and the actual production build.

10. DO NOT TRY TO FORCE GOOGLE

Do not add fake keywords or hidden text.

Do not add "ClipFlow" hundreds of times.

Do not use misleading structured data.

The goal is to make Google clearly understand:

ClipFlow
is a product by Cliy
at https://clipflow.cliy.me/

11. GOOGLE SEARCH CONSOLE

After making the changes, give me a checklist for Google Search Console:

- Inspect https://clipflow.cliy.me/
- Request indexing
- Submit https://clipflow.cliy.me/sitemap.xml
- Check Page Indexing
- Check URL Inspection
- Check rendered HTML
- Check favicon availability

Explain that Google may continue showing an old favicon/metadata temporarily because Google Search results are cached and recrawling is not instantaneous.

12. FINAL VERIFICATION

After making the changes, report:

A. Exact files changed
B. Exact metadata added/changed
C. Exact favicon location
D. Exact production favicon URL
E. Exact sitemap URL
F. Exact robots.txt URL
G. Exact canonical URL
H. Whether robots/noindex blocks Google
I. Whether the production build is clean
J. Any remaining issues

Most important:

DO NOT just tell me that the favicon exists in the source code.

Verify that the deployed production URL can actually serve the favicon and SEO assets.

Do not make unrelated changes.





